"Let $k,n,t$ be positive integers with $t\\leq k$, let $M(n,k)$ be the rectangle representation of $k$-multisets, and let $\\mathcal{M}(n,k,t)$ denote the families of $t$-intersecting $k$-multisets of $[n]$. **Meagher–Purdy conjecture.** If\n\n$$\nt(k-t)+2\\leq n\n$$\n\nand $\\mathcal{F}\\in\\mathcal{M}(n,k,t)$, then\n\n$$\n|\\mathcal{F}|\\leq\\binom{n+k-t-1}{k-t}.\n$$\n\nMoreover, if $n>t(k-t)+2$, equality holds if and only if every member of $\\mathcal{F}$ contains a fixed $t$-multiset of $M(n,k)$. This gives the paper’s proposed explicit threshold for the multiset Erdős–Ko–Rado bound; the paper’s abstract states that the numerical bound is established for this threshold, while the full equality assertion is the conjectural part recorded here."